# The #536 step 3 witness matrix, instance side, target `generic` (top-level extensions)
# (generated by tools/witness-matrix.py; the class side is
# witness_matrix_class/_generic/_abstract,
# the cross-cog column is in cogs.rs, the refusals in diagnostics.rs):
# conformance path x witness source x requirement x module arguments x
# scope of the extension, each cell printing what runs through a value
# typed `M` in a function at the top level (elsewhere, for a scoped
# extension), through one in the extension's module (where it is
# active), and for a direct call on a receiver typed as the conforming
# class where the extension is active. The expected output was computed
# from the rules, not taken from a run. For a class `K` that has `M`
# only through an extension `E` hanging from `C` on its chain, a call
# through `M` runs: (1) below `C`, the first method of `K`'s lookup order
# that replaces it (a subclass's own, one of a module it includes); (2)
# `E`'s own method; (3) the first of `C`'s own part of the order (its
# own methods, the modules it includes itself); (4) one of a module `E`
# includes after it; (5) the nearest in the included module's own
# ancestry; (6) the module's own body, an abstract one being implemented
# by what follows (a module `E` includes before it, an inherited
# method). For a module target, the including class's own method comes
# before the extension's. A direct call where the extension is active
# runs the extension's own method when it has one (chosen statically,
# also on a subclass's value typed as the class), else what the call
# through `M` runs. An own include (path `own`) goes by ordinary
# dispatch.
# Skipped as identical by the rules or not expressible:
# - path own: as the class target
# - paths sub_own_ext, ext_sub_inc: as the class target
# - the subclass paths beyond a reduced list: the same rule as path ext (one file per scope keeps the checker's time down)
# - the direct call column for args param x witness sup: as concrete
module M0
  abstract def m -> String
end
class C0[U]
  def initialize; end
end
extension C0[U]
  include M0
  def m -> String = "ext"
end
def up0(x: C0[Int]) -> M0 = x
def direct0(x: C0[Int]) -> String = x.m
def via0(x: M0) -> String = x.m
puts "generic/ext/ext/abstract/none/top: #{via0(up0(C0[Int].new))} #{via0(up0(C0[Int].new))} #{direct0(C0[Int].new)}"
module M1
  def m -> String = "M"
end
class C1[U]
  def initialize; end
end
extension C1[U]
